    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "466fff91_fc5ef2d6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903606
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-01T12:15:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Change is not intended to disable basic cooling device device objects. We only wanted to disable memory allocation of stats feature at https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/drivers/thermal/thermal_sysfs.c#909 and stats attribute group (at https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/drivers/thermal/thermal_sysfs.c#923 ) which exposes extra sysfs nodes under each cooling device to access this stats memory. \n\nThis is  the  same feature guarded under CONFIG_THERMAL_STATISTICS. So Upstream has already a way to disable this feature via defconfig. Now it is a restriction only in GKI right ?",
      "parentUuid": "bcb7a6ee_b76d71f6",
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d95ecf5f_ca0fb8be",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903606
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-01T12:15:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will update commit text why we need to disable it and explain memory footprint issue in next patchset.\n\nAs mentioned in bug, in our platform, more than 80+ cooling devices are there and internal slab memory consumption breakup shows that this feature is consuming  around 18.5MB memory and it is more critical for target variants with lower DDR memory config. We are looking for a way for vendor to disable this debugging feature for low DDR memory target variant.",
      "parentUuid": "81eff9cc_aa9a612b",
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2c77042_3bf6fb70",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-01T19:47:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The config option is a supported option that the upstream kernel community is supporting.\n\nYou are creating a brand new user/kernel api with this command line option, which is not something that upstream is willing to support, so that would push the requirement onto the Android kernel team to support it for forever going forwared.\n\nAnd I do not understand the need here, what exactly is taking up so much memory here that it is noticable vs. other kernel subsystems?  sysfs should be quite small if it is not being accessed (the memory is reclaimed as part of the inode/dentry cache.)  What is so special about this subsytem that is causing a lot of unneeded memory usage?\n\nRemember, sysfs attributes and the like work just fine with tens of thousands of devices on small 31 bit machines with no problems.  I find it odd that thermal attributes are somehow more expensive and noticeable than that common usage model.",
      "parentUuid": "466fff91_fc5ef2d6",
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7cb9af2_fe7b7ee3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903606
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-01T20:26:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here we are not talking about the memory used for sysfs node creation and all, instead this stats feature itself allocating a buffer for stats data collection at https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/drivers/thermal/thermal_sysfs.c#905\n\nEach the cooling device stats buffer depends on that device max mitigation level supported and based on this max level, it is creating multiple stat info buffer, including max level * max level two dimensional array buffer as well.\n\nIn our platform, multiple cooling devices will support upto 255 levels which could lead to huge memory buffer overall for this feature.",
      "parentUuid": "b2c77042_3bf6fb70",
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3a043b8_f56dc422",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-01T20:32:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then work on removing the run-time memory requirement for those statistics.  Why do they have to be created ahead of time?  Why not just look up the information when the sysfs file is read?\n\nAnd you seem to be ignoring the new user/kernel api here for some odd reason 😞",
      "parentUuid": "f7cb9af2_fe7b7ee3",
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b6173b6_3eb388cc",
        "filename": "drivers/thermal/thermal_sysfs.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 950,
      "author": {
        "id": 1105075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-28T17:56:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is fine, but why not make this configurable per cooling device? E.g. bring to upstream: and one of the option is to add a per cooling-device stats config in device tree to skip it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 941,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 950,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "243f6f183fa689d9212624592b8f4d203d4aaca3",
